// Wilhem_12_1_493             Salutations from Ecaterina the Wise.
// Josef_12_1_494              Wise? Not wise enough to protect the mortals from Cainite treachery. And neither was I.
// Wilhem_12_1_495             It has now been set right, by the courage of the Promethian Brujah!
// Josef_12_1_496              Has it? Another quarter of Prague is now defenseless before the fiends who steal innocents in the night. Sons of Caine and sons of Abel alike are missing. But I am pleased thou hast stopped the golem. Send my greetings to thy Mistress.
// Christof_12_1_497           Where do these many passages lead?
// Wilhem_12_1_498             Everywhere. Everywhere mortals live in Prague. There are secret entrances to even the most impregnable fortresses of the mortals.
// Christof_12_1_499           Most useful.
// Josef_12_1_500              Enter them not, stripling! Trespass, and I will peel thy pretty, unscarred face and wear it as a fair and tender mask. My tunnels are only for Nosferatu.
// Wilhem_12_1_501             Or those who pay the price.
// Christof_12_1_502           What price?
// Josef_12_1_503              Bring me a goblet of sweet blood from an elder Cainite of beautiful visage. Or venture not within my lair.
// Christof_14_3_546           Josef, do thy hidden tunnels allow vampires to enter the Cathedral?
// Josef_14_3_547              Aye. My tunnels undermine the sanctified ring of protection. I have used the tunnels to enter the Cathedral many times, and gorged myself upon the intoxicating Christian blood within.
// Christof_14_3_548           Then I shall bring thee the blood of a beautiful Cainite elder, and enter thy tunnels.


